  "content": "## Accessible meeting records\n\nWorkspace keys reach public workspace notes and spaces explicitly enabled for\nGranola API access. Folder permissions inherit their space's setting. They do\nnot grant unrelated private notes. Only notes with a generated AI summary and\ntranscript appear; a missing result does not establish that a meeting never\nhappened. The owner's private handwritten notes are null for workspace keys.\n\nDiscover actual note, folder and space IDs. API IDs use not_, fol_ and spa_\nprefixes; a web-link UUID, title or human name is not an API ID. Notes can\nbelong to several folders and spaces; folder parent_folder_id describes the\nhierarchy and space_id joins a folder to its space. Folder filtering includes\ndescendant folders. Null space_id can also mean an inaccessible space.\n\nOperation search searches the API contract, not meeting content. The REST API\noffers date, folder and space filters, with no natural-language meeting search.\nFilter accessible notes and inspect their contents to answer a topic question;\ndisclose the period and scope examined.\n\n## Transcript interpretation\n\nInline transcripts are optional. If including one fails with HTTP 413\n(TRANSCRIPT_TOO_LARGE), read note details without include and retrieve the\nseparate transcript endpoint through its complete continuation sequence. No\npartial transcript proves a complete quotation or count. An empty page can\nstill have a continuation; follow the returned paging state.\n\nSpeaker source describes the audio input, not a person's identity. macOS may\ndistinguish microphone from speaker audio. iOS currently uses microphone and\nmay supply anonymous diarization labels; do not invent attendee attribution.\nPreserve start/end timestamps when quoting. Summaries are AI-generated, so\nconfirm important wording against the transcript. Return only the relevant\npassages and identifying meeting metadata.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** while `page.hasMore` is true, continue with `page.nextCursor` unchanged. For `granola_api_details`, `granola_api_read`, `granola_api_search`, pass it as the top-level `cursor`; omit raw paging anchors on continuations. Keep the original method, path, filters, page size, fields and headers. The last page has no `nextCursor`. If `page.hasMore` is true without a cursor, the data is incomplete and continuation was withheld. When approaching execute_code's per-program call limit, return page.nextCursor before the call that would exceed it and continue in the next program; don't restart.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Hatch:** `granola_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `granola_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `granola_api_read` calls a reviewed read. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused. 13 operations are refused by design; use `granola_api_details` with the method and path to inspect the original operation summary and its separate refusal. Use details for refused methods outside the read/write call schemas; those methods remain unavailable.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. Writes take no idempotency key.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. An unknown id, or one these credentials cannot reach, fails as `connector_call_failed`; this API does not tell the two apart. It documents no conflict.\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.",
